WEBVTT

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.040
I'm glad it was just extended and not cancelled.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:12.300
I thought "Into Your Ears" was
going to be cancelled. I was so nervous.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.720
Kaibara-san does surprising things sometimes.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.620
He's not a bad person, though.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.390
I mean, he's actually a good person.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:21.430
Yeah.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:25.460
It's thanks to him that we're able
to be EARPHONES, after all.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.270
Yeah, of course!

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.690
Now that I think about it,

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:33.320
I haven't been to Classic Studio
since the last episode of Bodhisattvon.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.990
It's also been a while since the three of us all
went to the studio together in the morning.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.510
For some reason,
it already feels kind of nostalgic.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.730
The video I had to check over
for today was bad. It was really scary!

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:50.170
It was a lot of work looking up
all the hard words...

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:55.360
The words in mine weren't that hard,
but it took a really long time to just read it.

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:58.800
There were just so many scripts...

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.010
Oh, that's why you have that today.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:02.950
Yes.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.190
We're here!

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:43.990
<b>Blade Shining
game recording
Lucky Seven Life
audiobook recording
Cry of the Zombie:
The Devil's Bloody Legend</b>

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:46.780
Different work at the same studio...

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:48.410
It's a funny coincidence, huh?

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.790
It's a happy coincidence!

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.000
Futaba-san is dubbing a foreign film,

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:56.420
A foreign film is a movie from another country-koro.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:00.380
They're long, so they're sometimes
also called "long-running movies"-koro.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.970
lchigo has an audiobook,

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:06.890
An audiobook is when a book
is read aloud to be recorded-koro.

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:09.890
They're sold as CDs or downloads-koro.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:12.270
and Rin-chan's doing a game!

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.980
A game is...

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.400
a game-koro.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:20.400
It's my first time, so I'm really nervous.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.360
Me, too. But Rin-chan,
you're already used to it, right?

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.160
No, um...

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.990
This is my first time doing a game.

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:30.740
What, really?

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.100
Yes, actually.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:37.630
Wow, at the same studio, at the same time,

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:41.630
it's the first time we're
doing our respective jobs!

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:45.050
It's not coincidence anymore, it must be fate!

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:47.090
All right, let's do our best!

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:47.950
Yeah!

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:03.780
Shoes that don't make noise, check.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.240
Clothes that don't make noise, check!

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:09.140
Cellphone, off!

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:14.620
Today, I'm working with <i>that</i> person
again for the first time in a while.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.460
I have to be three times
more careful than usual.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.750
<i>That</i> person is...

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:19.980
Don't just stand there.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:20.820
Koro!
Don't just stand there.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:20.880
Don't just stand there.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:24.340
You're in the way.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:25.990
Hm? You?

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:31.450
If you can't even say a short line like that,
you're a failure as a seiyuu.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:34.520
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.480
Oh, good morning!

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.020
I am Ichinose Futaba from Aozora Production.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:41.070
I look forward to working with you today!

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:42.400
I know who you are.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.150
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.820
Don't let it growl during recording.

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:51.410
I'm sorry...

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:53.810
Yamori, you're strict, as usual.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.620
Oh, Koyama.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.690
Hey, long time no see.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:59.610
K-Koyama, as in...

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.290
Koyama Rikiya-san?!

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:06.300
I've been your fan for a very long time!

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:11.310
Randy from <i>Hard Guy</i> and Matt
from <i>Galaxy Wonder</i> were both wonderful!

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.430
I've watched everything since season one!

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:16.500
Of course, I have to seal away those feelings.

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:18.310
Nice to meet you.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:20.810
I am Ichinose Futaba from Aozora Production.

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:22.840
I look forward to working with you today!

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:26.590
Oh, I'm Koyama.
Look forward to working with you, too.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:29.610
Oh, Koyama-san!

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:34.660
Speaking of which, what happened in the new
season of <i>Hard Guy</i> was unexpected, huh?

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:35.520
<i>Hard Guy</i>?!

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:40.290
Yeah, I didn't think the main character,
Randy, would die right off the bat.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:41.000
Huh?!

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.070
And it was out of the blue in the first episode.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:44.940
What?!

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:48.630
Hm? Oh, did you hear that?

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.030
Y-Yes...

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:52.680
Oh, sorry about that.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:55.040
Didn't mean to spoil
the plot of the show for you.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.640
It's all right...

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:02.400
Well, please excuse me...

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:04.060
Okay, see you later.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:10.570
He spoiled it big time for me,
but then he apologized...

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:13.870
I don't know if I should be sad or happy...

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:19.500
Futaba-san, I'm glad you're having fun,
but you should switch to work mode soon-koro.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:23.790
That's right. I need to work hard.

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:29.380
When dubbing a foreign film,
even though it's still voice work,

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:33.930
the atmosphere is a little different
from an anime recording session-koro.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:39.160
Overall, everyone is older, and there
are a lot of actors from theater troupes-koro.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.840
For some reason, I feel really out of place.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:53.200
But it's all right
because I practiced a lot!

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:59.290
What a wonderful morning!

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:03.790
I've got fresh café au Iait
and my favorite donuts...

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:06.000
My cellphone is in a place I can reach easily,

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.920
I have manga that'll make me laugh,

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.990
and to soothe my heart, Korori-chan.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:14.090
Well, I guess I'll start my video check!

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.750
Come on...

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:23.890
Ashley (zombie)

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:24.020
Th-That just now was the character I play?
Ashley (zombie)

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:26.800
Ichinose Futaba
Th-That just now was the character I play?
Ashley (zombie)

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:26.810
Ashley (zombie)
Ichinose Futaba

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:34.570
l-l'll rewind... to 15:02...
The line is "Come here"...

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.510
Come on...

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:44.210
Oh, I forgot to say the line...

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:45.850
Come on...

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.290
One more time...

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.780
Come on...

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:55.510
Cry of the Zombie:
The Devil's Bloody Legend

00:07:56.220 --> 00:08:00.510
l-l-lt's okay. I'm <i>really</i> bad
with horror, but it'll be fine.

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:09.110
Besides, I'm in the same studio
as a senpai I respect.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.920
Concentrate, concentrate.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:13.440
Work, work.

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:18.490
Okay, let's start with the dry run for roll one.

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:23.910
Whoa, I'm getting nervous
just from putting the ears on.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:27.880
"Ears" are headphones-koro.

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:35.240
When dubbing a foreign film, they say the
Japanese lines while listening to the original-koro.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:38.700
I know, Tom's terrible!

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:42.140
He ate my apple pie without asking!

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:44.270
He ate my pizza, too.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:50.730
Wow, this is what it's like to hear the
Japanese and English at the same time.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:56.150
But it's kind of quiet...

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:57.650
Um, the volume control is...

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:00.760
Huh? What? What happened? Huh?

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:06.770
You're out of battery. Look, over there.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:07.160
Used
New

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:08.920
There are new batteries there.
Used
New

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:09.770
Used
New

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:09.790
Thank you very much!
Used
New

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:11.750
Thank you very much!

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:26.290
I just ran out of battery!

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:27.580
Mountain River       Lucky Seven Life    Moesaki Ichigo

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:31.290
I'll be fine!

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:35.300
I looked up the readings for the
kanji and where the accents go.

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:38.070
Okay, please start the dry run.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:38.980
Okay.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:47.410
In this world, there are those with extremely
good fortune, and those with bad fortune.

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:49.670
What is the difference between them?

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:53.130
Let's do a shumilation.

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:54.750
Stop for a sec.

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:55.420
Yes?

00:09:55.420 --> 00:10:00.240
Um, first of all, it's not
"shumilation," it's "simulation."

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:03.550
Huh? l-l'm sorry...

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:05.370
That's what it was...

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:11.190
And also, can you do it in a tone lower
and calmer than when you are in an anime?

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:12.670
Um, yes.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:16.150
I know you're the strawberry princess
from Planet Strawberry,

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:17.960
but can you be an earthling today?

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:19.300
Huh?!

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:21.820
H-How embarrassing...

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:24.320
I wasn't prepared enough at all.

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:29.290
But I can't believe the director
knew about Planet Strawberry!

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.910
I'm pretty happy about that.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:36.590
Okay, let's start with the system voice.

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:38.360
Yes, please.

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:43.550
Yes, that's right.

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:45.620
No, that's not it.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:47.370
It's fluffy!

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.460
It's lumpy.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.080
It's limp-

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:52.460
It's shiny-

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:54.210
It's soaked.

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:56.360
It's delicious!

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:58.280
It's going to explode.

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:03.660
What kind of situation is this?

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:09.620
Scripts for games sometimes
have everyone's lines,

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:13.060
but sometimes they only
have lines for your character-koro.

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:18.380
Hey, Nicola, have you decided
on your prom dress yet?

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:20.480
I don't even have a date yet, let alone a dress.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:25.640
In foreign films, you play a lot
of bit parts in addition to your role-koro.

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:26.720
Stop for a second.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:33.020
There's no problem with your acting,
but your voice qualities are too similar.

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:37.230
lchinose-san, can you try pitching it lower?

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:38.550
S-Sure.

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:46.010
Hey, Nicola, have you decided
on your prom dress yet?

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:50.160
Okay, great. Let's do it like that.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:53.000
All right, let's keep going.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:54.020
Okay!

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:06.430
Oh, that's how they make kissing sounds?

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:11.680
Oh no, there's no time for that.
It's almost Ashley's scene.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:19.980
Come... here...

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:24.420
Okay, that was the end of roll one.

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:26.090
Let's take a break.

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:30.620
Oh, you were scary.

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:43.490
Good work!

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.980
Oh, lchigo, you too.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.740
lchigo, your hair's flat!

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:51.720
Huh?

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:53.870
Yours is too, Futaba.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:54.850
Huh?

00:12:57.620 --> 00:13:01.620
Oh, even our breaks are at the same time, huh?

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:06.940
It's flat!

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:10.180
Headphones are scary!

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:12.930
I was so nervous.

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:18.970
Even though it's still voice work, the process
is completely different from anime recording.

00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:22.270
I was flustered when I first started, too.

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:26.860
I know what to do theoretically,
but actually doing it is hard.

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:30.920
You should stop sighing.

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:32.120
lchigo?

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:36.410
Sighs bring negative emotions.

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:39.630
That means you are bringing
unhappiness onto yourself.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:42.040
Ah, it's so hard!

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:45.710
It's hard to read it convincingly!

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:48.340
That was pretty convincing just now.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:48.840
Yes!

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:50.090
R-Really?

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:52.800
What about your game, Rin-chan?

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:54.970
Huh? Oh, yes.

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:56.730
Actually, I'm also having some issues...

00:13:57.180 --> 00:13:58.050
Hm?

00:13:58.050 --> 00:14:03.230
After this, I have to do three different
punch-receiving voices: big, medium, and small.

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:04.730
Huh? What's that?

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:09.400
Voices for when I receive
punches of different sizes.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:12.860
But, I'm not sure how to express
the strength of the punches.

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:14.950
Oh, that sounds hard.

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:18.010
Then, why don't we try it from "small"?

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:18.410
Huh?

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:21.400
Huh?!

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:23.800
W-Wait a minute, please stop!

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:26.420
Huh? You don't have to hold back.

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:28.920
It's not an issue of holding back...

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:32.220
Yeah, it's fine if it'll
help your performance, Rin-chan!

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:36.890
No, it's fine! l'll figure something
out with my imagination!

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:37.770
Really?

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:39.580
Really!

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:43.150
I should probably go back into the studio.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:45.100
I want to check my lines and stuff.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:46.060
Me, too.

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:48.650
Okay, let's work hard after this, too!

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:50.090
Yeah!

00:14:55.150 --> 00:15:00.410
I've heard that Koyama-san always
reads his script during break,

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:02.420
but I didn't think he'd be so focused...

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.830
What? Veggie juice?

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:09.840
And it's A Healthy Cup for
a Healthy Day Veggie Juice.

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:12.560
I imagined Koyama-san drinking...

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:20.020
something like this...

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:26.110
or something like this.

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:29.530
But he drinks veggie juice in real life, huh?

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:32.070
Is something the matter?

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:34.480
Oh, no! It's nothing!

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:38.660
Come on, come on. Work, work!

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:43.330
Don't worry. I'll definitely be back.

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:47.170
Let's watch the fireworks
on July 4th together this year, too.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:50.090
I read in an interview before:

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:58.630
When I do dubbing work, I'm always trying to
give a performance better than the original.

00:15:59.550 --> 00:16:03.850
There's a zombie here, too?
Damn, what's with them?

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:05.230
They just keep showing up!

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:07.160
Damn it!

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:12.980
Do you get it now, zombie bastards?

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:17.900
Now, let's start the best dinner party ever!

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:20.700
He <i>is</i> better! By a lot!

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:26.330
Who're you?

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:28.590
Those female zombies from earlier?

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:32.470
You guys should hurry up and go to sleep, too!

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:41.130
I can work in the same place as a senpai I've always admired.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:45.310
I'm so happy...

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:48.110
So very happy...

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:52.980
It's important to smile.

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:59.190
If all you do is sigh, then you will be
surrounded by other people who sigh.

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:03.200
If you always try to smile,
then you will have smiling friends;

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:06.330
in other words,
positive people will surround you.

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:09.410
Yeah, yeah, that's true!

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:09.860
That's really true!

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:11.940
Moesaki-san! Moesaki-san!
That's really true!

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:12.280
Moesaki-san! Moesaki-san!

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:14.330
Yes?

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:17.090
Are you reading this for yourself?

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:19.600
S-Sorry!

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:25.640
That part talks about the theme of this book,
so please try to emphasize it a little.

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:28.620
Okay, I get it.

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:32.400
All right! I have to focus!

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:36.990
Okay, let's move on to the
big, medium, and small punches.

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:38.090
Okay!

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:46.740
Okay, that's not bad.

00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:49.620
Can you make a little more of a difference
between big and medium?

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:51.090
Um, yes!

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:53.120
Big and medium...

00:17:57.670 --> 00:17:59.170
Take this!

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:06.340
Okay, let's do medium like that.
Try putting more feeling into big.

00:18:06.340 --> 00:18:08.060
Oh, okay!

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:12.850
We'll record a few different versions of
big and medium, so just keep doing them.

00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:13.830
Okay.

00:18:17.310 --> 00:18:21.410
It really is different acting
without anyone else around.

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:22.830
Take this!

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:27.530
That's really good! We've got it.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.000
I want ice cream!

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:31.770
You just had a hot dog, didn't you?

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:34.910
No, no! I want ice cream!

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:37.960
Ice cream, ice cream!

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:40.420
Your friends are important.

00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:47.140
Friends who want the same thing as you
and let you keep smiling will make you shine.

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:53.430
Don't worry! If we're together,
we can go anywhere!

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:56.440
That's right! We can do anything!

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:57.780
Okay, last scene.

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:02.030
Let's do the walla for the people
watching fireworks on July 4th.

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:03.010
Wow...

00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:09.510
Look!

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:23.260
Okay, that's a wrap. Thank you very much.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:24.480
Good work!

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:25.760
Good work today!

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:27.470
Good work today!

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:28.360
Good work.

00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:29.770
Good work today!

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:31.300
Good work to-

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:34.200
Looks like you've gotten
a little better, I guess.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:37.600
Thank you very much!

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:40.230
Yamori, you give compliments
occasionally, too, huh?

00:19:40.230 --> 00:19:41.110
Koyama-san!

00:19:42.270 --> 00:19:45.620
But I thought you really
did do a good job today.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:51.570
Thank you very much!
Thank you very much!

00:19:57.960 --> 00:19:58.960
Good work.

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:00.210
Good work today.

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:05.340
Oh, good work today.
Wow, we even finished at the same time!

00:20:05.340 --> 00:20:08.970
No, no. We were waiting for you.

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:11.230
We wanted to tell you, "Good work."

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:15.520
Oh, really? Thanks, you two!

00:20:15.970 --> 00:20:20.650
I just finished a little while ago,
but Rin-chan waited over an hour, you know.

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:26.220
Oh, it's all right! I was doing my summer
vacation homework while I waited, so it's fine.

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:28.160
Summer vacation homework?!

00:20:28.610 --> 00:20:30.240
How nostalgic...

00:20:30.240 --> 00:20:31.500
All of it is...

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:34.700
Rin-chan, you'll be in high school next year, right?

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:35.880
Oh, yes.

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:38.290
But your middle school has a joint high school,

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:39.920
so you don't need to take
an entrance exam, right?

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:43.170
Yes... I guess...

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:44.670
Hm?

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:47.380
Futaba-san, you have a wrap party after this, right?

00:20:47.380 --> 00:20:48.720
Oh, yeah.

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:51.680
Oh, you have wrap parties
after dubbing foreign films?

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:57.850
It's customary to have wrap parties after
each recording session for foreign films-koro.

00:20:57.850 --> 00:21:01.190
It's your chance to talk to your senpais-koro!

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:04.820
Yeah, so, sorry! I can't go home with you guys.

00:21:05.190 --> 00:21:06.610
It's all right, it's all right.

00:21:06.610 --> 00:21:08.950
Wrap parties are fun, aren't they?

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:13.250
Yeah! I'll walk you to the door.

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:20.500
It's raining.

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:23.260
It's the same as back then.

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:26.750
That day, we borrowed your umbrella, huh, Rin-chan?

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:30.050
Yeah, neither Futaba nor I had one.

00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:32.390
What about today?

00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:37.060
I guess we've changed a little, too.

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:38.770
Yeah, probably!

00:21:39.140 --> 00:21:42.100
Let's work harder from now on, too!

00:21:45.190 --> 00:21:47.440
Well, see you tomorrow, Futaba!

00:21:47.440 --> 00:21:49.030
See you at the radio recording!

00:21:49.360 --> 00:21:51.530
Yeah, see you later!

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:55.700
Come on, let's go to the wrap party.

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:04.130
Okay!

00:22:31.570 --> 00:22:34.560
Wow, seiyuu do a lot of different kinds
of work other than anime, huh?

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:36.700
So, let's try fighting with just our voices!

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:37.070
Go!

00:22:37.070 --> 00:22:37.580
Huh? What?!

00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:38.080
What, fight?

00:22:41.580 --> 00:22:42.870
I'll finish it with this!

00:22:42.870 --> 00:22:45.720
Evitation Final Bolderdeth!

00:22:46.540 --> 00:22:49.700
iroiro na koe no oshigoto
There are many different kinds of voice work

00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:53.760
dore mo oku ga fukai sekai da ne
There's a lot to know about each kind

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:57.090
takusan charenji shitai n desu
We want to try our hands at lots of them!

00:22:57.090 --> 00:22:58.930
Okay, let's move on to the request!

00:22:58.930 --> 00:23:03.140
From <i>Lyrical Nanoha A's,</i>
it's "Eternal Blaze"!

00:23:03.140 --> 00:23:06.260
toki o koe kizamareta
Engraved across space and time

00:23:06.260 --> 00:23:09.260
kanashimi no kioku
are memories of sadness

00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:12.300
massugu ni uketomeru
You, who unhesitatingly accepts them,

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:16.280
kimi wa hikari no tenshi
are my angel of light

00:23:16.280 --> 00:23:18.280
Now, let's get excited!

00:23:18.280 --> 00:23:20.160
One, two, three, go!
